MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Fire HD 10 feels like a plausible upgrade from my Fire 7 because a larger screen and more storage offer concrete benefits; I would choose the 64 GB version over the 32 GB option.",
    "A Fire TV Stick gives me a practical way to try streaming on my Samsung TV. I would consider the 4K stick, although my 720p screen would not benefit from its higher resolution, and I only need one streaming stick."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo displays and speakers assume I want voice control or video calling, but neither addresses a need shown by my camera, memory-card, and cable purchases.",
    "The smart plug and Echo Auto share a home or car setting with things I have bought, but I bought those accessories to connect, mount, or power devices, not to add Alexa automation."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Owning a Fire tablet seems to have been treated as interest in the wider Alexa family, when my interest is in what a particular device helps me do.",
    "My frequent electronics purchases seem to have been interpreted as a reason to suggest more gadgets, although many of those purchases serve specific accessory or connection needs."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of tripods, memory cards, a card reader, and a lens cap suggest that camera support and managing storage are recurring needs for me.",
    "Compatibility and useful improvements matter: an accessory needs to fit my existing equipment, a tablet upgrade needs a tangible benefit, and higher streaming resolution adds little on my current TV."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The suggestions recognized plausible tablet and TV upgrades but stretched my interest in practical electronics into an unsupported interest in Alexa devices."
}
